bailingmoe3: run the last layer's attention on the output rows only

The last layer's K/V go to the cache for every token, but prefill reads the attention result of the output row alone.
Selecting the rows before the attention instead of after it skips the work for the other rows. The result on the output
rows is exact. Ling-3.0, x86, 500 tokens at depth 1,300: 269 -> 279 tok/s; Pixel: part of the combined test in
docs/BENCHMARKS.md.

